---
/**
 * original-medicare-medigap-part-d-cost-estimator.astro
 * Tool: Medicare + Medigap + Part D Cost Estimator
 * Category: Medicare
 * Primary keyword: medicare medigap part d cost estimator
 * Supporting keywords: original medicare cost calculator 2026, medigap plan g plan n annual cost,
 *   medicare part b part d annual cost, how much does medigap cost per year
 *
 * URL: /tools/original-medicare-medigap-part-d-cost-estimator/
 * Title: Medicare + Medigap + Part D Cost Estimator | Seniors Audit   [58 chars]
 * Description: Free Medicare + Medigap + Part D cost estimator for 2026.
 *              See your annual range in seconds. No account needed.    [110 chars]
 *
 * CHANGES v2 (Aug 2026):
 *   - Age input replaced with date-of-birth (day/month/year) for accuracy
 *   - Age calculated client-side from DOB; never sent to server
 *   - Strategic internal contextual links added throughout form
 *
 * 2026 Verified Figures — re-confirmed against CMS on August 15 2026:
 *   Part B standard monthly premium : $202.90  [CMS 2026 Medicare Premiums Fact Sheet]
 *   Part B IRMAA surcharges /mo     : $81.20 / $202.90 / $324.60 / $446.30 / $487.00
 *   Part D national base premium /mo: $38.99   [CMS 2026 Part D Benefit Parameters]
 *   Part D IRMAA surcharges /mo     : $14.50 / $37.50 / $60.40 / $83.30 / $91.00
 *   Part B annual deductible        : $283     [CMS 2026 Medicare Premiums Fact Sheet]
 *   Part D OOP cap (2026)           : $2,100   [CMS 2026 Part D Benefit Parameters — confirmed $2,100]
 *   IRMAA single threshold (Tier 1) : >$109,000 (2024 MAGI)
 *   IRMAA joint threshold (Tier 1)  : >$218,000 (2024 MAGI)
 *
 *   Medigap premium ranges are illustrative industry-typical figures,
 *   clearly labeled as ESTIMATE — not from a government source.
 *   Source label: "Illustrative range — verify at medicare.gov/plan-compare"
 *
 * Compliance (Prompt 2 Section 0):
 *   ✓ No carrier or plan names
 *   ✓ No contact-info collection
 *   ✓ All calcs client-side only
 *   ✓ No fake urgency or dark patterns
 *   ✓ SHIP pathway for personalized help
 */

import ToolLayout from '@layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import NoSignupStatement from '@components/common/NoSignupStatement.astro';

const lastReviewed = 'August 2026';
const slug = 'original-medicare-medigap-part-d-cost-estimator';
const canonical = `https://www.seniorsaudit.com/tools/${slug}/`;

const US_STATES = [
  'Alabama','Alaska','Arizona','Arkansas','California','Colorado','Connecticut',
  'Delaware','Florida','Georgia','Hawaii','Idaho','Illinois','Indiana','Iowa',
  'Kansas','Kentucky','Louisiana','Maine','Maryland','Massachusetts','Michigan',
  'Minnesota','Mississippi','Missouri','Montana','Nebraska','Nevada',
  'New Hampshire','New Jersey','New Mexico','New York','North Carolina',
  'North Dakota','Ohio','Oklahoma','Oregon','Pennsylvania','Rhode Island',
  'South Carolina','South Dakota','Tennessee','Texas','Utah','Vermont',
  'Virginia','Washington','West Virginia','Wisconsin','Wyoming',
  'District of Columbia',
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How much does Original Medicare plus Medigap plus Part D cost per year in 2026?',
    answer: 'In 2026 the standard Medicare Part B premium is $202.90 per month ($2,434.80 per year). Adding a Medigap policy typically costs $1,800 – $4,920 per year depending on your plan, age, and state — this is an illustrative range, not a government-set figure. A Part D plan costs an average of $38.99 per month ($467.88 per year) plus drug expenses. Combined, most beneficiaries pay between $5,000 and $9,000 per year for full Original Medicare coverage before any IRMAA surcharges.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the difference between Medigap Plan G and Plan N?',
    answer: 'Medigap Plan G and Plan N both cover Part A costs and foreign travel emergencies. Plan G also covers the Part B deductible ($283 in 2026) and has no office or ER copays. Plan N does not cover the Part B deductible and charges up to $20 per office visit and $50 per emergency room visit (waived if admitted). Plan N typically costs $20–$50 per month less than Plan G. Plan G suits those who want fully predictable costs; Plan N may work if you rarely visit the doctor.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does Medicare Part B cost in 2026?',
    answer: 'The standard Medicare Part B monthly premium in 2026 is $202.90, or $2,434.80 per year. This is a fixed government-set amount published by CMS. If your 2024 Modified Adjusted Gross Income exceeded $109,000 (single filer) or $218,000 (married filing jointly), you pay an IRMAA surcharge of $81.20 to $487.00 per month on top of the standard premium. Social Security deducts this directly from your benefit payment.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I have to pay IRMAA on my Medicare premiums?',
    answer: 'IRMAA (Income-Related Monthly Adjustment Amount) applies when your 2024 Modified Adjusted Gross Income exceeded $109,000 for single filers or $218,000 for married couples filing jointly. Social Security uses your IRS tax return from two years prior. If your income has since dropped due to retirement, divorce, or another qualifying life event, you may appeal using SSA Form SSA-44, available at ssa.gov.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What does Medigap Plan G cover that Original Medicare does not?',
    answer: 'Medigap Plan G covers the 20% Part B coinsurance that Original Medicare leaves unpaid, the Part A hospital deductible and coinsurance, the Part B annual deductible ($283 in 2026), Part A hospice coinsurance, skilled nursing facility coinsurance, and foreign travel emergency care up to plan limits. With Plan G, your only regular out-of-pocket cost is the Part B deductible once per year.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does Medicare Part D cost in 2026?',
    answer: 'The 2026 national base Medicare Part D premium used for penalty and IRMAA calculations is $38.99 per month. Your actual plan premium varies by plan. If your 2024 income triggers IRMAA, add $14.50 to $91.00 per month. In 2026, the Part D out-of-pocket cap is $2,100 — once your covered drug costs reach that amount, you pay $0 for covered prescriptions for the rest of the year.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the Medicare Part D out-of-pocket cap in 2026?',
    answer: 'The Medicare Part D annual out-of-pocket cap in 2026 is $2,100. Once your total out-of-pocket spending on covered Part D drugs reaches $2,100 in a calendar year, you pay $0 for covered drugs for the remainder of that year. This cap was introduced by the Inflation Reduction Act and applies to all Medicare Part D beneficiaries regardless of which plan they choose.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I change my Medigap plan after I first enroll in Medicare?',
    answer: 'During your 6-month Medigap Open Enrollment Period — which begins the month you are both 65 or older and enrolled in Part B — insurers generally cannot use health underwriting to deny coverage or charge higher premiums due to pre-existing conditions (though premiums still vary by carrier, age, and pricing method). After that window closes, most states allow medical underwriting and insurers may charge more or deny coverage. Contact your free State Health Insurance Assistance Program (SHIP) counselor at shiphelp.org for guidance specific to your state.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the Medicare Part B deductible for 2026?',
    answer: 'The Medicare Part B annual deductible for 2026 is $283. You pay this amount once per calendar year before Medicare Part B begins paying its 80% share. Medigap Plan G covers this deductible entirely. Medigap Plan N does not — you pay $283 before your Part B benefits begin each year. This figure is published in the CMS 2026 Medicare Premiums Fact Sheet.',
  },
];

const howToSteps = [
  {
    name: 'Enter your age and state',
    text: 'Type your current age (60–85) and select your state from the dropdown. Your state affects Medigap premium ranges — some states regulate Medigap pricing more strictly, which can shift costs.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Select your Medigap plan preference',
    text: 'Choose Plan G, Plan N, or "Not sure yet." Plan G covers almost all out-of-pocket costs after Part B. Plan N costs a bit less but has small copays. Selecting "Not sure yet" shows a combined range spanning both plans.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Choose your prescription drug usage level',
    text: 'Select how many and what types of prescriptions you take: None, Low (1–2 generics), Moderate (3–5 mixed generic and brand), or High (specialty drugs or 6 or more medications). If unsure, choose Moderate as a starting point.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Indicate whether you expect to owe IRMAA',
    text: 'If your household 2024 income exceeded $109,000 (single) or $218,000 (joint), select Yes and choose your income bracket from the 2026 CMS table. Select "Not sure" for a baseline estimate without the surcharge.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Review your estimated annual cost range',
    text: 'Click "Estimate My Annual Cost" to see a full annual cost range broken down by Part B, Medigap, and Part D. Each line is labeled as FACT (verified government figure) or ESTIMATE (illustrative) so you know exactly what to verify.',
  },
];
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Original Medicare + Medigap Cost Estimator | Seniors Audit"
  description="Free Medicare + Medigap + Part D cost estimator for 2026. Calculate your combined monthly premiums, deductibles, and annual cost range in seconds."
  faqs={faqs}
  howToSteps={howToSteps}
  datePublished="2026-08-15"
  dateModified="2026-08-15"
  agency="CMS"
  canonical={canonical}
  keywords="medicare medigap part d cost estimator, original medicare cost calculator 2026, medigap plan g plan n cost, medicare annual cost estimate"
>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 3 — HERO
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="omm-hero">

    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="omm-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/medicare/" class="omm-bc-link">Medicare</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> › </span>
      <a href="/tools/" class="omm-bc-link">Free Tools</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> › </span>
      <span>Cost Estimator</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- H1 -->
    <h1 class="omm-h1">How Much Does Original Medicare + Medigap + Part D Cost Per Year?</h1>
    <p class="omm-date">Figures last verified against official sources in {lastReviewed}.</p>

    <!-- AEO Direct Answer Block (Section 3, element 3) -->
    <div class="omm-aeo-block" role="note" aria-label="Quick Answer">
      <p class="omm-aeo-label">Quick Answer</p>
      <p class="omm-aeo-text">
        In 2026, Original Medicare Part B costs <strong class="omm-gold">$202.90/month ($2,434.80/year)</strong> at the standard rate. Adding a Medigap policy typically costs an additional $1,800–$4,920/year (illustrative range), and a Part D plan averages $467.88/year in base premium. Most beneficiaries with standard income pay <strong class="omm-gold">$5,000–$9,000 per year</strong> total for comprehensive coverage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Problem Statement -->
    <p class="omm-problem">
      We noticed that most seniors approaching Medicare enrollment cannot find a single honest, plain-English estimate of what Original Medicare, Medigap, and a drug plan actually cost together each year — without being routed to an insurance agent or a lead-generation form. We built this free tool because you deserve a clear starting number in under three minutes, with every figure sourced and labeled so you know exactly what is a government fact and what is an estimate.
    </p>

    <!-- Who This Is For -->
    <ul class="omm-who-list" aria-label="Who this tool is for">
      <li class="omm-who-item"><span aria-hidden="true" class="omm-arrow">→</span> Seniors turning 65 who are comparing the full-year cost of Original Medicare plus Medigap to Medicare Advantage.</li>
      <li class="omm-who-item"><span aria-hidden="true" class="omm-arrow">→</span> Retirees with higher income who want to see how IRMAA surcharges change their total annual Medicare bill.</li>
      <li class="omm-who-item"><span aria-hidden="true" class="omm-arrow">→</span> Caregivers helping a parent or spouse build a retirement healthcare budget before choosing a Medigap plan.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 4 — NO SIGNUP POSITIONING STATEMENT
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <NoSignupStatement />

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 5 — THE TOOL INTERFACE
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="omm-tool-container" id="omm-tool-container" aria-label="Cost estimator form">

    <h2 class="omm-tool-h2">Estimate My Annual Medicare Cost</h2>

    <form id="omm-form" novalidate>

      <!-- Row 1: Date of Birth + State -->
      <div class="omm-field-group omm-field-full">
        <label class="omm-label">Your Date of Birth <span class="omm-required-hint">(used to calculate your age — affects Medigap premium range)</span></label>
        <div class="omm-dob-row">
          <div class="omm-dob-part">
            <label for="omm-dob-month" class="omm-dob-label">Month</label>
            <select id="omm-dob-month" name="omm-dob-month" class="omm-select" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="omm-dob-err">
              <option value="">— MM —</option>
              <option value="1">January</option>
              <option value="2">February</option>
              <option value="3">March</option>
              <option value="4">April</option>
              <option value="5">May</option>
              <option value="6">June</option>
              <option value="7">July</option>
              <option value="8">August</option>
              <option value="9">September</option>
              <option value="10">October</option>
              <option value="11">November</option>
              <option value="12">December</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="omm-dob-part">
            <label for="omm-dob-day" class="omm-dob-label">Day</label>
            <select id="omm-dob-day" name="omm-dob-day" class="omm-select" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="omm-dob-err">
              <option value="">— DD —</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="omm-dob-part omm-dob-year">
            <label for="omm-dob-year" class="omm-dob-label">Year</label>
            <input
              type="number"
              id="omm-dob-year"
              name="omm-dob-year"
              min="1939"
              max="1966"
              placeholder="YYYY"
              class="omm-input"
              aria-required="true"
              aria-describedby="omm-dob-err"
              autocomplete="bday-year"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="omm-age-display" class="omm-age-display" style="display:none;" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <span id="omm-dob-err" class="omm-field-err" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-field-group omm-field-full">
        <label for="omm-state" class="omm-label">Your State</label>
        <select id="omm-state" name="omm-state" class="omm-select" aria-required="true">
          <option value="">— Select your state —</option>
          {US_STATES.map(s => <option value={s}>{s}</option>)}
        </select>
        <p class="omm-field-hint">State affects Medigap premium ranges. Some states (New York, Massachusetts, Connecticut) regulate Medigap pricing differently — your actual quote may vary more from this estimate than in other states.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Medigap Plan Selection -->
      <fieldset class="omm-fieldset">
        <legend class="omm-legend">Medigap Plan You Are Considering</legend>
        <p class="omm-fieldset-hint">Not sure which plan to pick? Read our <a href="/medicare/medicare-supplement-plans-explained/" class="omm-inline-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">guide to Medigap supplement plans</a> or use the <a href="/tools/medigap-comparison-tool/" class="omm-inline-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medigap Plan G vs Plan N comparison tool</a> first, then come back here.</p>
        <div class="omm-radio-group" role="radiogroup" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="omm-plan-err">
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-plan" value="g" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content">
              <strong>Plan G</strong>
              <span class="omm-radio-sub">Covers the Part B deductible ($283) + all coinsurance — fully predictable annual costs</span>
            </span>
          </label>
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-plan" value="n" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content">
              <strong>Plan N</strong>
              <span class="omm-radio-sub">Lower monthly premium — but $20/office visit + $50/ER copays + does NOT cover the $283 deductible</span>
            </span>
          </label>
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-plan" value="unsure" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content">
              <strong>Not sure yet</strong>
              <span class="omm-radio-sub">Show me a cost range covering both plans — then I'll decide</span>
            </span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <span id="omm-plan-err" class="omm-field-err" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </fieldset>

      <!-- Plan N Copay Adjustments (hidden until Plan N selected) -->
      <div id="omm-plann-visits" class="omm-plann-section" style="display:none;" aria-label="Plan N visit estimates">
        <p class="omm-plann-note">Plan N has a $20 copay per office visit and a $50 copay per ER visit (waived if admitted). Adjust the defaults below to match your expected usage.</p>
        <div class="omm-row-two">
          <div class="omm-field-group">
            <label for="omm-office-visits" class="omm-label">Expected Office Visits per Year <span class="omm-default-hint">(default: 6)</span></label>
            <input type="number" id="omm-office-visits" name="omm-office-visits" min="0" max="52" value="6" class="omm-input" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
          <div class="omm-field-group">
            <label for="omm-er-visits" class="omm-label">Expected ER Visits per Year <span class="omm-default-hint">(default: 0.3)</span></label>
            <input type="number" id="omm-er-visits" name="omm-er-visits" min="0" max="10" step="0.1" value="0.3" class="omm-input" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Prescription Drug Usage -->
      <fieldset class="omm-fieldset">
        <legend class="omm-legend">Expected Prescription Drug Usage</legend>
        <p class="omm-fieldset-hint">
          Not sure what your drug costs will be? Read our <a href="/medicare/what-is-medicare-part-d/" class="omm-inline-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">guide to how Medicare Part D works</a>. For an exact drug cost comparison using your actual medication list, use Medicare's official <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="omm-inline-link">Plan Finder at medicare.gov/plan-compare</a>.
        </p>
        <div class="omm-radio-group" role="radiogroup" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="omm-drug-err">
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-drug" value="none" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content">
              <strong>None</strong>
              <span class="omm-radio-sub">No regular prescriptions — drug cost proxy: $0/yr</span>
            </span>
          </label>
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-drug" value="low" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content">
              <strong>Low</strong>
              <span class="omm-radio-sub">1–2 generic drugs — estimated drug cost proxy: $200–$500/yr</span>
            </span>
          </label>
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-drug" value="moderate" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content">
              <strong>Moderate</strong>
              <span class="omm-radio-sub">3–5 mixed generic and brand-name drugs — estimated drug cost proxy: $800–$1,500/yr</span>
            </span>
          </label>
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-drug" value="high" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content">
              <strong>High</strong>
              <span class="omm-radio-sub">Specialty drugs or 6+ medications — capped at 2026 Part D OOP limit: $2,100/yr</span>
            </span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <span id="omm-drug-err" class="omm-field-err" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </fieldset>

      <!-- IRMAA Question -->
      <fieldset class="omm-fieldset">
        <legend class="omm-legend">Do You Expect to Owe an IRMAA Surcharge in 2026?</legend>
        <div class="omm-irmaa-explainer" role="note">
          <p class="omm-irmaa-explain-text">
            <strong>What is IRMAA?</strong> IRMAA (Income-Related Monthly Adjustment Amount) is an extra monthly charge added to your Medicare Part B and Part D premiums if your income two years ago was above a certain level. It can add $81 to $487/month to your Medicare costs.
          </p>
          <div class="omm-irmaa-links">
            <a href="/medicare/irmaa-surcharge-explained/" class="omm-contextual-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">📖 Read: What is IRMAA and how does it work?</a>
            <a href="/tools/medicare-irmaa-calculator/" class="omm-contextual-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">🧮 Calculate your exact IRMAA tier first — then return here with your bracket</a>
            <a href="/tools/magi-for-medicare-calculator/" class="omm-contextual-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">📊 Not sure of your MAGI? Use the MAGI for Medicare calculator</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="omm-fieldset-hint">IRMAA applies if your 2024 Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) exceeded <strong>$109,000 (single)</strong> or <strong>$218,000 (married filing jointly)</strong>. MAGI = Line 11 of your Form 1040 + Line 2a (tax-exempt interest).</p>
        <div class="omm-radio-group" role="radiogroup" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="omm-irmaa-err">
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-irmaa" value="no" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content"><strong>No</strong> <span class="omm-radio-sub">My 2024 MAGI was at or below the thresholds above</span></span>
          </label>
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-irmaa" value="yes" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content"><strong>Yes</strong> <span class="omm-radio-sub">My 2024 MAGI was above the threshold — I'll select my income bracket below</span></span>
          </label>
          <label class="omm-radio-label">
            <input type="radio" name="omm-irmaa" value="notsure" class="omm-radio" />
            <span class="omm-radio-content"><strong>Not sure</strong> <span class="omm-radio-sub">Show me the baseline estimate without IRMAA added</span></span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <span id="omm-irmaa-err" class="omm-field-err" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </fieldset>

      <!-- IRMAA Bracket Selection (hidden until Yes selected) -->
      <div id="omm-irmaa-section" class="omm-irmaa-bracket-section" style="display:none;">
        <div class="omm-row-two">
          <div class="omm-field-group">
            <label for="omm-filing-status" class="omm-label">2024 Tax Filing Status</label>
            <select id="omm-filing-status" name="omm-filing-status" class="omm-select">
              <option value="single">Single / Married Filing Separately</option>
              <option value="joint">Married Filing Jointly</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="omm-field-group">
            <label for="omm-irmaa-bracket" class="omm-label">Your 2024 Income Bracket</label>
            <select id="omm-irmaa-bracket" name="omm-irmaa-bracket" class="omm-select" aria-describedby="omm-irmaa-bracket-hint">
              <!-- Populated by JS based on filing status -->
            </select>
            <span id="omm-irmaa-bracket-hint" class="omm-hint-text">Based on your 2024 tax return (Form 1040, Line 11 + Line 2a)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="omm-irmaa-info-box" role="note">
          <span class="omm-info-icon" aria-hidden="true">ℹ</span>
          IRMAA surcharges are deducted directly from your Social Security benefit payment. Figures are the 2026 official CMS surcharge amounts based on your 2024 MAGI (AGI + tax-exempt interest).
          Source: <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/basics/costs/medicare-costs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medicare.gov — 2026 Medicare Costs Overview</a>.
        </div>
        <div class="omm-irmaa-appeal-note" role="note">
          <span class="omm-info-icon" aria-hidden="true">💡</span>
          <strong>Did your income drop since 2024?</strong> You may be able to get your IRMAA surcharge reduced. Use our
          <a href="/tools/should-i-appeal-my-irmaa/" class="omm-inline-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRMAA appeal eligibility checker</a>
          or read about the
          <a href="/medicare/irmaa-surcharge-explained/" class="omm-inline-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SSA-44 appeal process</a>
          — then come back and re-run this estimate with your reduced bracket.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Submit Button -->
      <button type="button" id="omm-calc-btn" class="omm-btn-primary" aria-controls="omm-results">
        Estimate My Annual Cost
      </button>

    </form>

    <!-- ── RESULTS AREA ─────────────────────────────────── -->
