  <section class="omm-section" aria-labelledby="omm-action-heading" id="omm-action-plan">
    <h2 id="omm-action-heading" class="omm-section-h2">What to Do With This Result</h2>
    <p class="omm-section-intro">Your estimate is a starting point, not a finished answer. Here are the four specific actions to take next.</p>
    <ol class="omm-action-list">
      <li class="omm-action-item">
        <span class="omm-action-icon" aria-hidden="true">✅</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Verify your Part B and Part D IRMAA surcharge with Social Security.</strong>
          Log into your account at <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/myaccount/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ssa.gov/myaccount</a> and look for your Medicare Premium Determination letter. If you owe IRMAA, your exact surcharge is shown there. If your income has dropped since 2024, file <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/forms/ssa-44.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SSA Form SSA-44</a> to appeal.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="omm-action-item">
        <span class="omm-action-icon" aria-hidden="true">✅</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Get actual Medigap quotes for your ZIP code at medicare.gov/plan-compare.</strong>
          The Medigap premium in this tool is an illustrative national range. Actual premiums vary by as much as $100/month between insurers in the same ZIP code for identical coverage. Comparing at least three quotes is strongly recommended. <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Go to medicare.gov/plan-compare →</a>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="omm-action-item">
        <span class="omm-action-icon" aria-hidden="true">✅</span>
        <div>
          <strong>If you chose Plan N, mark your Part B deductible date.</strong>
          The $283 Part B deductible resets every January 1. After your first covered service of the year, Part B begins paying its 80% share. Plan N's $20 office copay applies after the deductible is met. Budget $283 at the start of each calendar year.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="omm-action-item">
        <span class="omm-action-icon" aria-hidden="true">✅</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Compare Part D plans annually — your drug list, not just the premium, drives the real cost.</strong>
          Use the <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medicare Plan Finder</a> to enter your actual drug list and see total estimated drug costs — not just the monthly premium — for every plan in your ZIP code. The Annual Enrollment Period runs October 15 – December 7.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="omm-action-item">
        <span class="omm-action-icon" aria-hidden="true">✅</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Call a free SHIP counselor to review your specific situation.</strong>
          Your State Health Insurance Assistance Program (SHIP) provides free, unbiased counseling — no commissions, no insurance affiliations. Dial <strong>1-877-839-2675</strong> or find your local counselor at <a href="https://www.shiphelp.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">shiphelp.org</a>.
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="omm-action-footer">This checklist gets you moving — your final numbers should always come from <a href="https://www.medicare.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medicare.gov</a>, <a href="https://www.ssa.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SSA.gov</a>, or a SHIP counselor.</p>
  </section>


  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 6 — HOW TO USE THIS TOOL
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="omm-section omm-section-tinted" aria-labelledby="omm-howto-heading">
    <h2 id="omm-howto-heading" class="omm-section-h2">How to Use This Tool — Step by Step</h2>
    <ol class="omm-steps-list">
      <li id="step-1">
        <strong>Step 1 — Enter your age and state.</strong>
        Type your current age (between 60 and 85) and select your state from the dropdown. Your state affects Medigap premium ranges — some states like New York, Massachusetts, and Connecticut regulate Medigap pricing differently, which can shift your actual cost.
      </li>
      <li id="step-2">
        <strong>Step 2 — Select your Medigap plan preference.</strong>
        Choose Plan G, Plan N, or "Not sure yet." Plan G covers almost all out-of-pocket costs after Part B pays its share. Plan N costs a bit less per month but has small copays per visit. If you are still comparing, select "Not sure yet" to see a range covering both options side by side.
      </li>
      <li id="step-3">
        <strong>Step 3 — Choose your prescription drug usage level.</strong>
        Select the tier that best describes how many and what types of prescriptions you take: None, Low (1–2 generics), Moderate (3–5 mixed), or High (specialty drugs or 6 or more). If you are not sure, choose Moderate as a reasonable middle ground. This affects the drug-cost portion of your estimate only — it does not change your Part B or Medigap figures.
      </li>
      <li id="step-4">
        <strong>Step 4 — Indicate whether you expect to owe IRMAA.</strong>
        If your household income in 2024 exceeded $109,000 (single filer) or $218,000 (married filing jointly), select "Yes" and pick your income bracket from the official 2026 CMS table. If you are not sure, select "Not sure" — the tool shows your baseline estimate without the surcharge so you can still see the floor of your cost.
      </li>
      <li id="step-5">
        <strong>Step 5 — Click "Estimate My Annual Cost."</strong>
        Your full annual cost range will appear below the button, broken down by Part B, Medigap, and Part D. Each line is labeled FACT, ESTIMATE, or DECISION SUPPORT so you know exactly which figures to verify before making any enrollment decision.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <!-- Pro Tip -->
    <div class="omm-pro-tip" role="note">
      <p class="omm-pro-tip-title">💡 Pro Tip — Your Medigap Open Enrollment Window Is the Most Important Date in Medicare</p>
      <p class="omm-pro-tip-text">
        Your 6-month Medigap Open Enrollment Period begins the month you are <em>both</em> age 65 and enrolled in Part B. During this window, insurers must sell you any Medigap plan at standard rates regardless of your health history. After the window closes, most states allow medical underwriting — meaning you could be charged more or denied coverage for pre-existing conditions. Read our guide on <a href="/medicare/medicare-vs-medicare-advantage/" class="omm-link">understanding your Original Medicare vs Medicare Advantage options</a> before your window closes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>


