      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="omm-sources-note">Medigap premium ranges shown in this tool are illustrative national typical ranges based on industry pricing patterns — they are not from a government source and are clearly labeled as ESTIMATE throughout. Actual Medigap premiums vary by insurer, age, state, and health status. Always get actual quotes at <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/plan-compare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">medicare.gov/plan-compare</a>.</p>
    <p class="omm-independence">Seniors Audit is an independent educational platform. We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to any government agency, insurance company, or financial services firm. All government-set figures use the official formulas and current amounts published by the agencies listed above. We do not receive payment for referrals, leads, or any action taken by visitors to this site.</p>
  </section>


  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 10 — FAQ
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="omm-section omm-section-tinted" aria-labelledby="omm-faq-heading">
    <h2 id="omm-faq-heading" class="omm-section-h2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="omm-faq-list">

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">How much does Original Medicare plus Medigap plus Part D cost per year in 2026?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">In 2026 the standard Medicare Part B premium is $202.90 per month ($2,434.80 per year). Adding a Medigap policy typically costs $1,800 – $4,920 per year depending on plan, age, and state — this is an illustrative range, not a government-set figure. A Part D plan costs an average of $38.99 per month ($467.88/year) in base premium, plus prescription drug costs. Combined, most beneficiaries pay between $5,000 and $9,000 per year for comprehensive coverage before any IRMAA surcharges.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">What is the difference between Medigap Plan G and Plan N?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">Medigap Plan G and Plan N both cover Part A costs and foreign travel emergencies. Plan G also covers the Part B deductible ($283 in 2026) and has no office or ER copays. Plan N does not cover the Part B deductible and charges up to $20 per office visit and $50 per ER visit (waived if admitted). Plan N typically costs $20–$50 less per month than Plan G. Plan G suits those who want fully predictable costs; Plan N may work if you rarely visit the doctor.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">How much does Medicare Part B cost in 2026?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">The standard Medicare Part B monthly premium in 2026 is $202.90, or $2,434.80 per year. This is a fixed government-set amount published by CMS. If your 2024 Modified Adjusted Gross Income exceeded $109,000 (single filer) or $218,000 (married filing jointly), you pay an IRMAA surcharge of $81.20 to $487.00 per month on top of the standard premium. Social Security deducts this directly from your monthly benefit check.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">Do I have to pay IRMAA on my Medicare premiums?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">IRMAA (Income-Related Monthly Adjustment Amount) applies when your 2024 Modified Adjusted Gross Income exceeded $109,000 for single filers or $218,000 for married couples filing jointly. Social Security uses your IRS tax return from two years prior. If your income has since dropped due to retirement, divorce, or another qualifying life event, you may appeal using SSA Form SSA-44, available at ssa.gov.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">What does Medigap Plan G cover that Original Medicare does not?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">Medigap Plan G covers the 20% Part B coinsurance that Original Medicare leaves unpaid, the Part A hospital deductible and coinsurance, the Part B annual deductible ($283 in 2026), Part A hospice coinsurance, skilled nursing facility coinsurance, and foreign travel emergency care up to plan limits. With Plan G, your only regular out-of-pocket cost is the Part B deductible once per year — after that, you pay nothing for Medicare-covered services.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">How much does Medicare Part D cost in 2026?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">The 2026 national base Medicare Part D premium used for penalty and IRMAA calculations is $38.99 per month. Your actual plan premium varies by plan and ZIP code. If your 2024 income triggers IRMAA, add $14.50 to $91.00 per month. In 2026, the Part D out-of-pocket cap is $2,100 — once your covered drug costs reach that amount, you pay $0 for covered prescriptions for the rest of the year.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">What is the Medicare Part D out-of-pocket cap in 2026?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">The Medicare Part D annual out-of-pocket cap in 2026 is $2,100. Once your total out-of-pocket spending on covered Part D drugs reaches $2,100 in a calendar year, you pay $0 for covered drugs for the remainder of that year. This cap applies to all Medicare Part D beneficiaries regardless of which plan they choose, and was established by the Inflation Reduction Act as verified in the CMS 2026 Part D Benefit Parameters document.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">Can I change my Medigap plan after I first enroll in Medicare?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">During your 6-month Medigap Open Enrollment Period — which begins the month you are both 65 or older and enrolled in Part B — you can buy any Medigap plan at standard rates regardless of health. After that window closes, most states allow medical underwriting, and insurers may charge more or deny coverage. A free SHIP counselor at shiphelp.org can advise on your specific state's rules at no cost.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="omm-faq-item">
        <h3 class="omm-faq-q">What is the Medicare Part B deductible for 2026?</h3>
        <p class="omm-faq-a">The Medicare Part B annual deductible for 2026 is $283. You pay this amount once per calendar year before Medicare Part B begins paying its 80% share. Medigap Plan G covers this deductible entirely, so Plan G holders have no Part B deductible exposure. Medigap Plan N does not cover it — you pay $283 out of pocket before Part B benefits begin each calendar year.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


